; ==============================================================================
; Bootstrapped Lin compiler -- entry point
; ==============================================================================
; Stage 1 of the self-host: this program is the compiler.  The C engine runs it
; (see bin/lin-boot); the only services it takes from the host are the ones a
; program is entitled to -- reading its input and printing -- and the source text
; arrives in LIN_BOOT_SRC because the language has no argv accessor yet.
;
; NOT YET A COMPILER.  What is here today is the entry point and the contract;
; the front end (reader -> AST -> net) and the .line emitter are the work in
; docs/BOOTSTRAP-PARITY.md.  It exits non-zero with nothing on stdout so
; test/parity.py reports BOOT-DIFF instead of mistaking silence for agreement.
; ==============================================================================

(load "std/std.lin")

(ffi.exit 70)
